relude, safepoint, lowering or import programs runs the generator in the same slice | P2 |\\\\\\\\n43:| Refinement of the row above, with the decisive assertion text: the Python recursion guard does not fire before the JVM stack gives out. `yang.python.antlr.e2e-test/recursion-under-real-hooks-test` (e2e_test.clj:819) expects `#:py{:exception {:type \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RecursionError\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", :args [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"maximum recursion depth exceeded\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]}}` and gets `[:thrown \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"java.lang.StackOverflowError\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`. Reproduced on jupiter (independent host, no other lane) and shiva at 6d6b7e71; green on the macOS dev machine. The safepoint/linked-safepoint variants surface the same exhaustion inside `Continuation.hasheq` while hashing the state. So the three remaining yang.python slow reds are ONE root: the guest recursion depth the limit allows exceeds what a default JVM thread stack sustains on Linux `| CLOSED 2026-11-02 (6fae7fbe): the JVM default `ThreadStackSize` is 2048 KB on macOS and 1024 KB on Linux, and the guest code runs on a CREATED thread (raising `ulimit -s` to 64 MB does not help; `-J-Xss32m` makes the failing test pass 1/5/0 on jupiter). Run the affected JVM test lanes with an explicit `-Xss` of at least 2 MB, or make the guard measure remaining stack instead of a fixed depth; done — the `:test` alias now carries `:jvm-opts [\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"-Xss4m\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"]`, and every JVM lane inherits it `| yin.vm (recursion guard / thread stack) with the yang.python e2e evidence `| refinement found while verifying the link-reds landing (the engineer's macOS-green counts do not reproduce on Linux) | P2 (closed 2026-11-02: all seven namespaces green on Linux) |\\\\\\\\n47:| the interactive Dart entry (`dart run bin/yin_repl_main.dart`) fails to COMPILE under the current Flutter selection (mise.toml selects Flutter `latest` on beta): a material `Color resolved = switch (...)` API mismatch — pre-existing (the (host) diff tou