eiver-admission\\\\\\\\n+  (let [sender-record {:yin.admit/id \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"sender-only\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n+                       :yin.admit/decision :allow\\\\\\\\n+                       :yin.admit/asserters #{'sender}\\\\\\\\n+                       :yin.admit/address :sender-only}\\\\\\\\n+        source (update-in (support/parked-installer)\\\\\\\\n+                          [:installs 'host.mod :response] merge sender-record)\\\\\\\\n+        wire (support/lift source nil)\\\\\\\\n+        address (jing/segment-key (:manifest (support/module-response)))\\\\\\\\n+        recv (support/new-machine)\\\\\\\\n+        task (rows/decode wire)\\\\\\\\n+        install (first (nth (:slots task) 12))]\\\\\\\\n+    (is (not-any? #(contains? (nth (:slots install) 3) %) (keys sender-record)))\\\\\\\\n+    (let [carried (update-in task [:slots 12 0 :slots 3] merge sender-record)\\\\\\\\n+          {:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\\\\\\\\n+          refusal (error #(rows/lower-task recv (rows/emit carried) attach!\\\\\\\\n+                                            support/installer-lower-opts))]\\\\\\\\n+      (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-response]\\\\\\\\n+             ((juxt :yin.k/status :yin.k/kind) refusal)))\\\\\\\\n+      (is (zero? @count)))\\\\\\\\n+    (doseq [opts [{} {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'other.mod address}}\\\\\\\\n+                  {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'host.mod :wrong-address}}\\\\\\\\n+                  {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'host.mod nil}}]]\\\\\\\\n+      (let [{:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\\\\\\\\n+            refusal (error #(rows/lower-task recv wire attach! opts))]\\\\\\\\n+        (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal)))\\\\\\\\n+        (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod address}} (:yin.k/missing refusal)))\\\\\\\\n+        (is (zero? @count))\\\\\\\\n+        (is (empty? (:installs recv)))))\\\\\\\\n+    (let [{:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\\\\\\\\n+          restored (rows/lower-task (assoc recv :attach-stream attach!) wire attach! {:yin.k/admitted-modules {'host.mod address}})\\\\\\\\n+          response (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :response])\\\\\\\\n+          child (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :vm])\\\\\\\\n+          wait (first (:wait-set child))]\\\\\\\\n+      (is (pos? @count))\\\\\\\\n+      (is (= install (first (nth (:slots (rows/decode (support/lift restored nil))) 12)))\\\\\\\\n+          \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"relift reproduces the carried install row\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")\\\\\\\\n+      (is (not-any? #(contains? response %) (keys sender-record)))\\\\\\\\n+      (stream/append! (get (:resources child) (:stream-id wait)) :resume)\\\\\\\\n+      (let [done (vm/run restored)\\\\\\\\n+            installed (module/module-entry (:modules (:modules done)) 'host.mod)]\\\\\\\\n+        (is (= 42 (:value done)))\\\\\\\\n+        (is (= address (:address installed)))\\\\\\\\n+        (is (not (contains? installed :admission)))))))\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:2873:  `:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}` option, default empty, and\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3191:- Invariant: One occurrence has at most one admitted holder, and each\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md:3320:   names a carried record. Both wire phases running/parked are admitted,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md:715:requires composition-supplied `:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}`\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:529:| P2 | (`:wait`) the pending's reason is admitted by `inst(pc−1)` (act) or `inst(site)` (tail): `:stream-next → :next`; `:stream-put → :put`; `:ffi-call → :ffi, :ffi-request`; `:call → :next :put :ffi :ffi-request :link-request :link-response :install`; `:park` and `:current-continuation` admit none (frozen §4.1; `wire-of-kind`, `handoff.cljc:491-504`; ucf-revisions §8) | `:reason-mismatch` |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:569:admitted canonical frames. Two kernels are intended to reconstruct\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:750:an admitted carrier value (:prim). The current de Bruijn register\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:987:the chain's names\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", which drops `x` entirely, and the lowered de Bruijn\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1266:the `[:lit nil]` of row 22 dropped → `:window-missing`; a `:reified`\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1766:…}` (§4.2). A primitive function is an admitted carrier value (`:prim`);\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1815:`opts {:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}}`. The default is empty:\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:1821:`:yin.k/admitted-modules` option to the lower. The lift never carries the sender's\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2103:   slot; a primitive is an admitted carrier value (`:prim`) that the\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2144:    4's two admitted pairs are asserted by count. **Amended 2026-10-13\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2151:    for a unique dead slot, `:window-missing` for a dropped live slot),\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2350:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"`lift(lower(frame)) = frame` holds for admitted canonical frames, as\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2570:root is admitted exactly as a version-0 body is, proposes nothing, and\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2653:| B3 | §5.2 refusal rows; §8.2 item 7 | the `:tail` fourth slot is `:row-shape` at structure step 2, and the tamper is a raw row edit with rehash | the row table fixes `:tail` at three slots before S1 runs; `emit` drops extra abstract slots silently |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2692:| D4 | §4.2, §7.2, §8.3 item 6 | a primitive is an admitted carrier value; the register kernel refuses one in its payload `:yin.k/unsupported :continuation-registers` with the path before attach; \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"is no carrier value\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" withdrawn; four refusal fixtures | engineer deviation 8, codex D4: the limit is the receiver's, not the carrier's |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2698:| R3 | §6.3, §7.2 | a closure or continuation in the free environment is refused on the native lanes both ways (`:free-env-value`), admitted by the carrier and the reference lane; nested values included | codex F1: no finite canonical form through the shared free environment; refuse, do not convert |\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2762:  `:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}` before attaching any stream,\\\\\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2840:  R3) and admitted everywhere else. If any real composition seeds a de\\\\\\\\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRunning tests in #{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"test\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"}\\\\\\\\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTesting yin.vm.ucf.holder.export-test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/1793560000000-engineer-module-pins-r2a.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:36:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_18\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tail -8 /tmp/module-pins-r2a-focused.log; rg -n 'serve-table' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc; git diff -- docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nTesting dao.jing.hash-registry-contract-test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTesting dao.jing.mem-test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTesting dao.jing.stream-test\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nTesting yin.vm.linker-manifest-test\\\\\\\\n11:   The streams carry no random identity and `serve-table` answers s0, s1\\\\\\\\n133:(defn serve-table\\\\\\\\n370:  (try (rows/lift-task machine (serve-table) (lift-opts header))\\\\\\\\ndiff --git a/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md b/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md\\\\\\\\nindex 7a26313b..353ae4d6 100644\\\\\\\\n--- a/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md\\\\\\\\n+++ b/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md\\\\\\\\n@@ -710,3 +710,13 @@ Code: `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc` (38-47, 265-273, 339-351);\\\\\\\\n `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc` (113, 167, 171, 450, 605-616, 713);\\\\\\\\n `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc` (375-395);\\\\\\\\n `src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc` (153-158, cited by UCF 7.3.2).\\\\\\\\n+\\\\\\\\n+**2026-10-16, I-8 (module-pins slice, partial; R4 only).** Lower now\\\\\\\\n+requires composition-supplied `:yin.k/admitted-modules {name manifest-address}`\\\\\\\\n+for every carried install child, default empty, before attaching streams;\\\\\\\\n+the lift never carries the sender's admission decision fields; a carried\\\\\\\\n+admission field is refused as `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`. No row shape or\\\\\\\\n+fixture address changes in this partial slice. The module-pin carrier,\\\\\\\\n+host-profile schema and their fixture re-mint are blocked pending the\\\\\\\\n+Architect's decision on where host-module export profiles are recorded.\\\\\\\\n+No compatibility promise is added.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\ncollab/1793560000000-engineer-module-pins-r2a.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:51:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_25\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"command_execution\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tail -5 /tmp/module-pins-r2a-focused.log; sed -n '1878,1904p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"aggregated_output\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"counterexample-search incidence families 100 states: {:numbered 74, :refused 26, :max-work 421748} failures: 0\\\\\\\\nSKIP host-collapse: slash-crossed identifiers remain distinct on JVM\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nRan 648 tests containing 18431 assertions.\\\\\\\\n0 failures, 1 errors.\\\\\\\\n      :halted (when (seq waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\\\\\\\n      :blocked (when (empty? waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\\\\\\\n      :parked (when-not (some #(= parked-id %) (take-nth 2 (:slots parked)))\\\\\\\\n                (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :parked-id {}))\\\\\\\\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\\\\\\\\n    (run! #(check-install! recv %) installs)))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- check-install-admission!\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Carried children require the receiver composition's explicit name/address\\\\\\\\n   admission. Sender admission evidence never authorizes a receiver install.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  [task opts]\\\\\\\\n  (doseq [inst (nth (:slots task) 12)]\\\\\\\\n    (let [[mn _ _ response] (:slots inst)\\\\\\\\n          address (jing/segment-key (:manifest response))]\\\\\\\\n      (when-not (= address (get (:yin.k/admitted-modules opts) mn))\\\\\\\\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil\\\\\\\\n                  {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {mn address}}})))))\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n(defn- check-closure!\\\\\\\\n  \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"A closure row names a :closure tuple of its carried vector: the entry\\\\\\\\n   (:closure-origin) and that tuple's binders (:closure-binders), as\\\\\\\\n   lower-closure will demand.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n  [code c]\\\\\\\\n  (let [[a entry params] (:slots c)\\\\\\\\n        v (get code a)\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndbe9e072:collab/yin-vm/1793620000000-engineer-module-pins-r2d.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:14:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_5\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793550000000-architect-module-pins-review.report.md'\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"Completed-GMT: 2026-10-16 06:06:47 GMT\\\\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-16 13:06:47 +07\\\\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\\\\nSession-ID: pending\\\\nRole: Architect (read-only; worktree datomworld-srvm-pins, branch srvm-module-pins @ 6df441d0, 13 uncommitted files)\\\\nBrief: collab/1793540000000-architect-module-pins-review.prompt.md\\\\nInputs: collab/1792130530811-engineer-module-pins.report.md, collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md (§4.2, §4.4, §6), the full `git diff`, and the sources cited below.\\\\n\\\\n# Module pins: Part A review of R4, Part B ruling on host-module pins, Part C round-2 steps\\\\n\\\\n## Part A: review of the uncommitted R4 part\\\\n\\\\n### A.0 What was checked\\\\n\\\\n- Gate placement: `check-install-admission!` (`rows.cljc:1883-1892`) runs in `lower-task` after `check-custody!` and before `attach-streams!` (`rows.cljc:2301-2304`), over every task of `task-tree` (`rows.cljc:1805-1808`, root and every nested install child, pre-order). Refusal throws before the first attach: the attach-count law holds (tests assert zero attaches).\\\\n- Paths that lower install children: only `rows/lower-task`. Backends (`layout/lower-task`) refuse `:installs` already; `remote.cljc:485` lowers no installs; fork packs go through the same `lower-task`; `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` now forwards `:yin.k/admitted` (`export.cljc:539`); the holder driver's two lower paths are discussed in P2-1.\\\\n- Other copies of the sender's admission: `engine/link-install` (`engine.cljc:1436-1443`) is the only consumer of the four `:yin.admit/*` response fields outside the linker; nothing else reads the installed entry's `:admission` (grep over `src`: only `linker/admission.cljc`, `linker/interpreter.cljc`, `yin.repl` configuration, none read `(:admission entry)`). Dropping rather than replacing is safe for consumers.\\\\n- Refusal shape: `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` matches threat-model §4.4 exactly (no `:yin.k/kind`, no `:yin.k/discovery`). The carried address can never be nil at this point because `check-install!` already required a manifest map (`rows.cljc:1846-1851`), so `{'host.mod nil}` in the admitted map correctly refuses.\\\\n- Mutants: all three are meaningful (name-only acceptance, retained sender admission, gate bypass) and each is killed by distinct assertions. Mutant 2 has to be re-done after P1-1 (see below).\\\\n- Tests: portable (plain data, keyword sentinel addresses, host-neutral catch forms, kondo clean per the engineer). Fixtures admit their fixed manifests explicitly from the composition side (`rows_support.cljc:298-301`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:349-352`), never derived from the pack.\\\\n- Docs: continuation §2.5 and §7.1 (\\\\\\\"the lower does not re-discharge free names\\\\\\\") are unchanged and still true, since the pin work has not landed. UCF §7.6.4/§7.6.5 are unchanged spec text. The §7.11 row, continuation Q5, revisions I-8 and the known-gaps rows say \\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\" for the pin carrier: no overclaim. The claims that are wrong after P1-1 are listed under P3-3.\\\\n\\\\n### A.1 Findings\\\\n\\\\n**P1-1. Dropping the sender's admission at restore breaks fenced recovery and the relift law for every real pack with an install child.**\\\\nThe lift copies the install record's `response` whole into the `:install` row (`install-node`, `rows.cljc:1643`). The linker's interpreter puts `:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision`, `:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address` on every successful DHT-admitted response (`interpreter.cljc:416-421`), so a real pack's `:install` row carries them. The new restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2236-2237`) then produces a machine whose `:installs` response lacks the four keys. Consequences:\\\\n- `rehydrate-fenced` re-prepares and re-encodes the restored machine and demands byte equality with the published pack (`export.cljc:548-556`); the relift's install row now differs from the carried one, so every fenced recovery of such a pack answers `:yin.k/undecodable :recovery-inconsistent`.\\\\n- The harness law \\\\\\\"the relift equals the lift by root\\\\\\\" (`safepoint_harness_test.cljc:10`, asserted at `:629` via `canonical-under`) fails for the same packs.\\\\nThe current tests pass only because every fixture response (`rows_support/module-response`, `blocking-body`) carries no `:yin.admit/*` keys. This is a correctness defect, not a test gap.\\\\nRequired fix (revert-not-fix does not apply, this is the slice's own line): strip the four `:yin.admit/*` keys **at lift**, in `install-node`, so the pack never carries S's decision (\\\\\\\"the carrier narrows, never widens\\\\\\\", §4.1), and make the lower **refuse** a carried response that still carries any `:yin.admit/*` key as `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` (one clause in `check-install!`'s existing `and`; hand-crafted packs only). Delete the restore-side `dissoc`. Then the restored response equals the carried one, fenced reproduction and the relift law hold by construction, and `link-install` sees no sender record. New pin for the mutant: a source whose install response carries the record lifts to an `:install` row without the keys (assert on the decoded row's slot 3), and a pack with the keys spliced back in is refused before attach with zero attaches. Keep the existing \\\\\\\"installed entry has no `:admission`\\\\\\\" assertion.\\\\n\\\\n**P2-1. The holder driver has no seam to supply `:yin.k/admitted`, so the composition's real lower path refuses every pack with an install child.**\\\\n`driver/lowered` is called with `{:exclusive true}` (`driver.cljc:2294`) and with the grant map (`driver.cljc:1588-1600`); the fenced recovery at `driver.cljc:2455-2457` passes only `:address` and `:attach`. None forwards an admitted map. This is fail-closed (safe) but it means R4 as written makes carried install children unreachable through the holder, with no driver test noticing (`driver_test.cljc` has no install-child handoff; `:2726` fakes one for gate-mode only). Required for round 2, not for landing R4 alone: a config entry `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))` forwarded by `lowered` and by the fenced recovery call (two lines), plus one driver test that lowers a parked-installer checkpoint with and without the config. Until then, a known-gaps row \\\\\\\"holder driver passes no admitted-modules map; install-child handoff through the driver refuses\\\\\\\" (P2) must land with R4.\\\\n\\\\n**P2-2. `:yin.k/admitted` already means two other things in the same vocabulary.**\\\\nIt is a ledger fact kind, \\\\\\\"one effect's dedup record with its result\\\\\\\" (`ledger.cljc:22, 115, 553`), and the driver's not-holder answer field for the admitted variant set (`driver.cljc:743, 1655`). The threat model (§4.4, my text) chose the word carelessly. Rename the lower option to `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, the five test files and the five doc amendments. Cheap now, a permanent vocabulary defect after commit.\\\\n\\\\n**P3-1. The gate reports one child, not the complete set, and omits `:yin.k/discovery`.**\\\\nEvery other `:yin.k/unsatisfied` from the lower carries `:yin.k/discovery` (`rows.cljc:1629, 1686, 1923, 1930`). §4.4's shape omitted it; §4.2's has `:complete`. Ruling: in round 2 fold the admission gate into the single `check-modules!` stage (Part C step 5), which collects every unlisted child of the tree and every unsatisfied pin into one `:yin.k/missing` map with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. Not blocking for landing R4 alone; the §4.4 shape is acceptable until then.\\\\n\\\\n**P3-2. Name-keyed admission across the tree.** The admitted map is flat by module name over the whole tree. A nested child that installs the same name as a sibling at another address cannot be admitted. The registry family makes this a degenerate case; note it in the `lower-task` docstring, no code.\\\\n\\\\n**P3-3. Doc statements to retarget after P1-1.** Continuation §7.2 amendment (\\\\\\\"Restore drops the sender's …\\\\\\\"), Q3 amendment (\\\\\\\"drops the sender's admission evidence on restore\\\\\\\"), `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2333-2335`, transport-tuples amendment (\\\\\\\"Restore drops the sender's four …\\\\\\\"), revisions I-8 (\\\\\\\"restore drops\\\\\\\"), known-gaps R4 row (\\\\\\\"sender admission dropped on restore\\\\\\\"). All become \\\\\\\"the lift never carries the sender's admission fields; a carried one is `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`\\\\\\\". Also replace `:yin.k/admitted` by the P2-2 name in all five docs.\\\\n\\\\n**P3-4. `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` docstring** says \\\\\\\"default empty\\\\\\\" twice in different words; fine. No change needed.\\\\n\\\\nVerdict for Part A: **CHANGES-REQUIRED** (P1-1 blocking; P2-2 rename and the P2-1 ledger row land with it; P3-1/P3-2 deferred to round 2).\\\\n\\\\n## Part B: ruling on host-module (\\\\\\\"nil\\\\\\\") pins\\\\n\\\\n### B.0 Facts the ruling rests on\\\\n\\\\n- A host-registered entry has `:address nil` and lists its exports as `:yin.module/primitives {sym profile-address}` (`register-host-module`, `module.cljc:223-263`). `module/host-export-profile` answers exactly that profile address for a qualified symbol (`module.cljc:266-281`): a **keyword** `:yin.k.pp/blake3-…` minted by `vm/primitive-profile` over `{name class arities effects host-state}` (`vm.cljc:338-356`). Plain data, no functions, no host objects. The core `stream` and `cell` modules are host modules with literal cljc profiles and `:none` host-state (`module.cljc:350-363, 405-410`), so their addresses are identical on JVM, Node and Dart.\\\\n- The linker already defines \\\\\\\"satisfied by equal profile\\\\\\\" for exactly this case: `declared-discharge` discharges a primitive obligation by `(= profile (module/host-export-profile modules name))` (`linker.cljc:1014-1018`), and a module obligation by equal manifest address (`:1022-1027`). UCF §7.6.5 already carries `:yin.k/primitives {name <expected profile>}` in the outcome.\\\\n- The lift's `discharge!` answers a qualified free name by registry presence (`rows.cljc:1611-1616`) and nothing of the entry travels. The task row's `requires` slot is a plain map (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), so two more keys cost no slot change.\\\\n\\\\n### B.1 Ruling\\\\n\\\\n1. **Host modules participate in this slice.** Not deferred. Reason: `stream` and `cell`, the most common modules in any pack, are host modules; deferring leaves R6 (silent skew) open for the common case while closing it only for DHT-linked modules. The data is already pure, the comparison already exists in the linker, and the lift already resolves the entry. The risk of implementing is one more `requires` key and a fixture re-mint, both owed anyway for `:yin.k/modules`. The risk of deferring is a second re-mint later and a documented hole in the fetch-loop contract.\\\\n\\\\n2. **What the lift records.** Only what the live code uses: for every live free name `ns/f` that `discharge!` answered through the registry (`rows.cljc:1614-1616`, after `E`, store, primitives and installing names, which stay as they are):\\\\n   - `:yin.k/modules` gets `{ns <manifest address>}` when the entry is linked (`(:address entry)` non-nil), `{ns nil}` when it is host-registered;\\\\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports` gets `{ns/f <profile address>}` when the entry is host-registered, the value being `(module/host-export-profile (:modules m) 'ns/f)`.\\\\n   Not all exports. Recording all exports would refuse a receiver whose host module gained or changed an export the code never touches, and it would persist what the free-name scan already derives. A lift where `host-export-profile` answers nil for a name the registry claims to hold (an entry with a malformed `:yin.module/primitives`) is `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile {:yin.k/name ns/f}`.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Canonical encoding.** Two maps in the task row's `requires` beside `:yin.k/segments`, `:yin.k/trees` and `:yin.k/cursor-profiles`: `:yin.k/modules {symbol -> string-or-nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {qualified-symbol -> keyword}`. Keys sorted by the carrier's existing rules for symbol keys; the `keyed`/`built` host-collapse discipline applies (module names contain dots, no slash; a qualified export has one slash, so the known P3 `keyed` gap does not reach these maps, but add the count guard anyway as the `built` precedent). Absent maps are not emitted when empty (same as `:yin.k/trees` with no segments is still emitted; follow whatever the existing `requires` does for empties, byte-stable). No richer value in `:yin.k/modules`: a tagged vector `[:host profiles]` beside address strings mixes value kinds in one slot and duplicates the primitives precedent for no gain.\\\\n\\\\n4. **How the lower compares** (new `check-modules!`, one pass over the whole tree, after `check-custody!`, before `attach-streams!`, absorbing today's `check-install-admission!`):\\\\n   - `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`: receiver's `module/resolve-module` entry exists with `(= address (:address entry))` → satisfied. Entry exists with another address (including a host entry, nil, where a linked one was pinned, or vice versa) → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :module-pin-mismatch :yin.k/name ns :yin.k/pinned address :yin.k/linked (:address entry)}`, the `:dependency-pin-mismatch` words (`engine.cljc:1388-1393`). Entry absent → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns address}}`.\\\\n   - `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`: `(= profile (module/host-export-profile (:modules recv) 'ns/f))` → satisfied. Receiver answers another profile → **terminal** `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/kind :host-export-mismatch :yin.k/name ns/f :yin.k/pinned profile :yin.k/held <receiver's>}`. Receiver answers nil (no such export, or the module is absent, or it is linked rather than host) → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}}` (the `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` entry will be in the same map when the module is absent).\\\\n   - Receiver's host module exporting **more** than the pin names: satisfied (subset by construction, since only used exports are pinned). Equality is of profile addresses, never of normalised profile maps: the address already covers name, class, arities, effects and host-state.\\\\n   - Carried install children: `:yin.k/admitted-modules {ns address}` equality as today; unlisted → collected into `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {ns carried-address}}`.\\\\n   - Order: terminal mismatches are thrown first (nothing the composition can fetch repairs them), then one collected refusal `{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied :yin.k/discovery :complete :yin.k/missing {…}}` with keys present only where something is missing. Zero attaches in every case.\\\\n   - The fetch loop (composition, not this slice) requires only keys of `:yin.k/missing :yin.k/modules` whose pin is non-nil; a nil pin and every `:yin.k/host-exports` entry are composition prerequisites and are not fetched.\\\\n\\\\n5. **Determinism across hosts.** Profile addresses are BLAKE3 content hashes over plain data computed identically on all three hosts (the same mechanism Stage E already pins for primitives); manifest addresses are segment keys. The refusal maps are plain data. Pin T8 in `stage_e_rows_test.cljc`: a `requires` with both maps re-encodes byte-identically and the two terminal refusals and the collected refusal are `=` across JVM, Node and Dart.\\\\n\\\\n6. **Threat-model text amended by this ruling.** §4.2's shape gains `:yin.k/host-exports`; \\\\\\\"whose export profiles equal those the lift recorded\\\\\\\" becomes \\\\\\\"whose profile address for each used export equals the pinned one\\\\\\\"; §4.4's option is renamed `:yin.k/admitted-modules` and its refusal is folded into the collected shape with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`. T4 reads: a nil pin plus `:yin.k/host-exports` is satisfied by a host module answering equal profile addresses for the pinned exports; another profile for a pinned export refuses `:host-export-mismatch`; a missing export is collected as missing; extra exports are ignored.\\\\n\\\\n### B.2 Alternative considered and rejected\\\\n\\\\n\\\\\\\"Refuse nothing for nil pins, document, defer\\\\\\\": `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` would then only assert \\\\\\\"a host module of this name must exist\\\\\\\", which `resolve-var` already enforces at run time, and skew in `stream`/`cell` profiles between two compositions would still run under R's authority (R6, R8 for the common case). The saving is one map and one lift line; not worth a second re-mint. Rejected.\\\\n\\\\n## Part C: ordered steps for codex round 2\\\\n\\\\nPreconditions: worktree `datomworld-srvm-pins`, the current 13 files uncommitted. `npm ci` and `mise trust` are done there. Per-iteration verification is `bb test:clj`; full three-host `bb test` once at the end, one lane set at a time, foreground only. Read `docs/agents/build-n-test.md` first. No `collab/` path is ever staged.\\\\n\\\\n**Commit 1 (R4, lands alone): fix P1-1, rename P2-2, ledger P2-1.**\\\\n1. `rows.cljc` `install-node`: `response` → `(dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)` before the `cbor/encode` check and the row. Delete the restore-side `dissoc` (`rows.cljc:2233-2237` and its comment).\\\\n2. `rows.cljc` `check-install!`: add to the existing `and` of the `:install-response` clause `(not-any? #(= \\\\\\\"yin.admit\\\\\\\" (namespace %)) (filter keyword? (keys response)))`.\\\\n3. Rename `:yin.k/admitted` → `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in `rows.cljc`, `export.cljc`, `rows_support.cljc`, `rows_test.cljc`, `rows_custody_test.cljc`, `export_test.cljc`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc`.\\\\n4. Tests in `rows_test.cljc` `carried-install-requires-receiver-admission`: keep every assertion; add (a) the decoded wire's root `:install` row slot 3 has none of the four keys, (b) the harness-style relift of the lowered machine is `=` by root to the wire (reuse `canonical-under` or compare the install row), (c) a pack with the four keys spliced into the install row refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` with zero attaches. In `export_test.cljc`: a frozen parked-installer whose source response carried the sender record rehydrates `:ok` and reproduces the pack byte for byte (this is the P1-1 regression pin).\\\\n5. Mutants (run, record counts, restore): (m1) lift keeps the sender keys → 4(a), 4(b)/export pin fail; (m2) `check-install!` accepts `:yin.admit/*` keys → 4(c) fails; (m3) gate bypass → as before.\\\\n6. Docs (P3-3 list): reword \\\\\\\"dropped on restore\\\\\\\" to \\\\\\\"never carried by the lift; a carried one is refused\\\\\\\", rename the option, add the known-gaps row for P2-1 (holder driver seam, P2) and the P3-2 docstring note. Revisions I-8 wording likewise.\\\\n7. `bb test:clj`, kondo on changed files, `git diff --check`. Report; Architect sign-off; commit `fix(yin.vm.ucf): carried install children need receiver admission; lift never carries sender admission` (format.md convention, no Co-Authored-By).\\\\n\\\\n**Commit 2 (pins carrier + lift + lower + driver seam): the ruling.**\\\\n8. `rows.cljc` lift: in `discharge!` (or a sibling collector over the same `answered?` walk), record for every live registry-answered name the entry: linked → `:yin.k/modules {ns address}`; host → `:yin.k/modules {ns nil}` and `:yin.k/host-exports {ns/f profile}`; nil profile → `:yin.k/non-portable :host-export-profile`. Put both maps into `requires` (`rows.cljc:1687-1689`), sorted, empty maps handled as the existing `requires` keys handle empties.\\\\n9. Encoder/decoder/validator: `requires` is a plain map today, so confirm `check-dependencies!` (`rows.cljc:1918`) still accepts the two extra keys and add the key-count guard for symbol keys as in `built`. Malformed-slot collection: non-map `:yin.k/modules`, non-symbol key, non-string-non-nil value, non-keyword `:yin.k/host-exports` value, unqualified `:yin.k/host-exports` key → `:yin.k/undecodable :requires` (extend the existing kind, no new kind).\\\\n10. `rows.cljc` lower: replace `check-install-admission!` by `check-modules!` per B.1 item 4 (terminal mismatches first, then one collected refusal with `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, zero attaches), same position (after custody, before attach). Delete `check-install-admission!`.\\\\n11. Driver seam (P2-1): `driver/lowered` and the fenced recovery call forward `(:yin.k/admitted-modules (:config state))`; `rehydrate-fenced` already forwards. One driver test with and without the config over a parked-installer checkpoint.\\\\n12. Tests (threat model §7.1, amended): T1 (lift of harness row 17 emits `{:yin.k/modules {host.mod nil} :yin.k/host-exports {host.mod/f <profile>}}`; a DHT-linked fixture emits `{pym.k <address>}`; names answered by `E`, store, prims or module stores emit nothing), T2 (receiver lacking the module: collected refusal, `:discovery :complete`, zero attaches), T3 (linked module at another address: `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both; equal address lowers), T4 (B.1 item 6), T5 (already in commit 1, re-point to the collected shape), T8 (Stage E cross-host row), T9 (layering: `rows.cljc` requires neither `linker.interpreter`, `linker.dht` nor `dao.lease`), T10 (`resolve-var` unchanged). T6/T7 (fetch loop, lease) are composition work, out of this slice; leave their known-gaps rows.\\\\n13. Mutants (run, record, restore): lift records all exports instead of used; lower compares by name presence instead of address; lower accepts a different profile address; lower reports `:incomplete`; attach before `check-modules!`. Each must be killed by a named test.\\\\n14. Fixture re-mint: `rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` and any ledger/Stage E fixture whose `requires` now carries the two maps; record old → new addresses in the report and in `yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` (I-8 completes, dated). C4 scanner pins are untouched (AST-level; see the standing note).\\\\n15. Docs: continuation §2.5 (binding fact travels: the two maps), §7.1 step 6 (records address or host profile), §7.2 dependencies row (module check, three refusal kinds, delete \\\\\\\"the lower does not re-discharge\\\\\\\"), §11 Q5 closed as C with the host-export ruling, Q3 (admitted set is `:yin.k/admitted-modules`); UCF §7.6.4 (add the host-export sentence), §7.6.5 (add `:yin.k/host-exports` to the outcome), §7.11 row updated; transport grammar (`requires` slot: the two maps); `yin.vm.linker.dht.md` 7.5.11 amendment reworded; threat-model report is a collab artifact, not edited; known-gaps: Q5 row → landed, R4 row → landed, P2-1 row → closed by step 11.\\\\n16. `bb test:clj` per iteration; at the end `bb test` all three hosts (foreground, one lane set at a time; \\\\\\\"Testing <ns>\\\\\\\" must appear in Node output); kondo; `git diff --check`. Report with counts, mutant kills, old → new addresses. Architect sign-off, then commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf): module pins and host-export pins in requires; lower re-discharges by equal address and profile` and, if the driver seam is separable, a third commit `feat(yin.vm.ucf.holder): admitted-modules config forwarded to the lower`.\\\\n\\\\nCommit split summary: (1) R4 alone, after the P1-1 fix and the rename; (2) carrier + lift + lower + tests + re-mint + docs; (3) optional driver seam if it would otherwise delay (2).\\\\n\\\\nCHANGES-REQUIRED (Part A)\\\\nRULING-READY\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\\ndbe9e072:collab/yin-vm/register-vm-2026-10.MANIFEST.txt:1:1791540000000-architect-srvm-phase4-design-r2.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log\\