ev/jolt_workload_w.clj\\\\\\\\nD\\\\\\\\tsrc/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj\\\\\\\\nD\\\\\\\\ttest/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj\\\\\\\\nD\\\\\\\\ttest/d2_wedge_probe2.clj\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/call/conformance.clj\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/clojure_test.clj\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/cross_lang_test.clj\\\\\\\\nD\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/latte_oracle/h3_2_a_verify.clj\\\\\\\\nD\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/latte_oracle/h3_2_fixture_family.md\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_evidence.edn\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_unexercised.edn\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\\\\\\\\nM\\\\\\\\ttest/yang/python/antlr/e2e_test.clj\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_16\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"**REJECT for landing.** The round 3 gate still treats an ordinary source map as a cell reference based on its public shape.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nAt [clojure.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1224), a three-entry map with `:type :cell-ref`, `:id`, and any 64-character string for `:seal` passes the structural test. For example, invoking such a map with `:id` should return its stored value, but the routing at [line 1343](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:1343) sends it to admission, which calls `cell/get` at [line 2184](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:2184). The VM rejects the invalid seal or nonexistent cell instead of performing the map lookup. The seal prevents a capability bypass; it does not establish ordinary map semantics.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nGenuine issued references have the tested shape and continue through admission to the common invoker when their cell contains a callable entry. But the claimed distinction between genuine and non-genuine references is not made by the shape check: [the VM issues references as maps](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc:316), and authenticity is established separately against the heap and seal.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe new tests at [cross_lang_test.clj](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cljrt/test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj:161) concretely assert `42n` for the stated literal and local-binding cases, but both examples have four entries and a three-character seal. Neither exercises a format-matching three-entry map. The \\u201cruntime-built\\u201d case also binds a literal rather than constructing the map through runtime operations.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nThe round 3 diff touches only the two stated files. Its hunks leave the accepted globals-lifecycle and kind-of changes, token-packet authentication, arity guard, witness admission, VM files, and `yang/core/call.cljc` unchanged; I found no call-node surgery, foreign `:code` extraction, or wrappers in that diff.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nOne landing qualification: locally, `git merge-base d3a35830 8fb525c4` is `7eb7fc9e`, so the reviewed head does not contain the landed master merge. The quoted checks are accepted as reported, but they do not by themselves establish the behavior of the eventual merge result. No dynamic checks were run in this review.\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"turn.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"input_tokens\\\\\\\":206587,\\\\\\\"cached_input_tokens\\\\\\\":173568,\\\\\\\"cache_write_input_tokens\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"output_tokens\\\\\\\":1879,\\\\\\\"reasoning_output_tokens\\\\\\\":176}}\\\\nDISPATCH_RC=0\\\\n\\\",\\\"exit_code\\\":0,\\\"status\\\":\\\"completed\\\"}}\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"severity\": \"P3\",\n      \"category\": \"Debug\",\n      \"file_path\": \"collab/yang-clojure/1794310000000-reviewer-cljrt-r4.codex.stdout.log\",\n      \"line_number\": 25,\n      \"message\": \"Leftover debug statement detected.\",\n      \"snippet\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"item.completed\\\",\\\"item\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"item_11\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"command_execution\\\",\\\"command\\\":\\\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\\\\\"sed -n '150,205p' test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj && sed -n '2050,2150p' test/yang/clojure_test.clj && rg -n '8\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\.10|conformance' docs/design\\\\\\\"\\\",\\\"aggregated_output\\\":\\\"\\\\n(deftest clojure-source-cell-ref-map-invocation-test\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a source map {:type :cell-ref} is ordinary invocable data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; The donor's exported function invokes its own source map literal:\\\\n    ;; the map lookup answers 42, where the structural cell test used to\\\\n    ;; dereference the map as a cell and fail the VM.\\\\n    (is (= {:js/out [\\\\\\\"42n\\\\\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\\\n           (xl/call [:clojure\\\\n                     \\\\\\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :marker 42} :marker))\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [:typescript \\\\\\\"console.log(probe());\\\\\\\"]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a source map with the full forged cell-ref shape is ordinary invocable data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; The map spells every key of an issued reference among its own\\\\n    ;; entries; it is still data, so the lookup answers 42 where key\\\\n    ;; presence alone used to dereference it and fail the VM.\\\\n    (is (= {:js/out [\\\\\\\"42n\\\\\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\\\n           (xl/call [:clojure\\\\n                     \\\\\\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :customer :seal \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wax\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :marker 42} :marker))\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [:typescript \\\\\\\"console.log(probe());\\\\\\\"]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a full-shape three-entry map with a valid-format 64-char seal is ordinary invocable data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; The exact issued format \\u2014 three entries, a seal string of the issued\\\\n    ;; length \\u2014 with an :id the engine's heap could never have minted (heap\\\\n    ;; ids are :cell-N keywords): the map can never be a reference, so the\\\\n    ;; invocation is the map lookup and answers the stored seal string,\\\\n    ;; where the shape gates of the previous rounds routed it to admission\\\\n    ;; and the dereference refused the VM.\\\\n    (is (= {:js/out [(str \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" (apply str (repeat 64 \\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\")) \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")], :js/uncaught nil}\\\\n           (xl/call [:clojure\\\\n                     (str \\\\\\\"(defn probe [] ({:type :cell-ref :id :some-key \\\\\\\"\\\\n                          \\\\\\\":seal \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"} :seal))\\\\\\\")]\\\\n                    [\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [:typescript \\\\\\\"console.log(probe());\\\\\\\"]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a runtime-built full-shape map (assoc-constructed, not a bound literal) invokes as data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; The map is assembled by assoc at runtime, so no literal ever holds\\\\n    ;; it; the shape test runs on the constructed value and the lookup\\\\n    ;; still answers the stored seal string.\\\\n    (is (= {:js/out [(str \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\" (apply str (repeat 64 \\\\\\\"a\\\\\\\")) \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")], :js/uncaught nil}\\\\n           (xl/call [:clojure\\\\n                     (str \\\\\\\"(defn probe [] (let [m (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :type :cell-ref) \\\\\\\"\\\\n                          \\\\\\\":id :some-key) \\\\\\\"\\\\n                          \\\\\\\":seal \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")] \\\\\\\"\\\\n                          \\\\\\\"(m :seal)))\\\\\\\")]\\\\n                    [\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [:typescript \\\\\\\"console.log(probe());\\\\\\\"]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a runtime-built map with the forged cell-ref shape is ordinary invocable data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= {:js/out [\\\\\\\"42n\\\\\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\\\n           (xl/call [:clojure\\\\n                     \\\\\\\"(defn probe [] (let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :customer :seal \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"wax\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" :marker 42}] (m :marker)))\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [\\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\"]\\\\n                    [:typescript \\\\\\\"console.log(probe());\\\\\\\"])))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest python-function-kind-of-in-typescript-test\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"js/kind-of over a cell-backed foreign callable is :function\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= {:js/out [\\\\\\\"function\\\\\\\"], :js/uncaught nil}\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The value of the single expression `form`, or the raw error outcome.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [form]\\\\n  (let [[tag payload] (run-library [form])]\\\\n    (if (= :yin.k/ok tag) payload [tag payload])))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(def ^:private cell-modules\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The library lane's host surface with the `cell` module registered, so a\\\\n   spliced `cell/new` can mint genuine references (the engine seals them\\\\n   under the test composition's capability secret).\\\\\\\"\\\\n  (module/register-cell-module library-modules))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(defn- run-cell-probe\\\\n  \\\\\\\"The value of running the compiled probe program with `node` spliced into\\\\n   the marker operand \\u2014 `(probe <node>)` keeps its call-site routing \\u2014 on\\\\n   one lane, or the thrown refusal's ex-data.\\\\\\\"\\\\n  [node lane]\\\\n  (let [ast (walk/postwalk\\\\n              (fn [n] (if (= n (u/v 'marker-operand)) node n))\\\\n              (yang/compile-program\\\\n                (into (yang/library-for '[(defn probe\\\\n                                            [m]\\\\n                                            (m :type))])\\\\n                      '[(defn probe\\\\n                          [m]\\\\n                          (m :type))\\\\n                        (probe marker-operand)])\\\\n                true\\\\n                library-opts))]\\\\n    (try\\\\n      (run-guest-ast ast cell-modules lane 1000000)\\\\n      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\\\\n        [:thrown (select-keys (ex-data e) [:reason :effect])]))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest test-common-call-cell-ref-map-invocation\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a full-shape data map with a 64-character seal is ordinary invocable data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; The map spells every key of an issued reference and the seal has the\\\\n    ;; issued format; its :id names nothing in the engine's heap id language\\\\n    ;; (:cell-N), so it can never be genuine and its invocation is the map\\\\n    ;; lookup, on both evaluators, where the previous rounds' shape gates\\\\n    ;; routed it to admission and the dereference refused it.\\\\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :cell-ref]\\\\n           (run-library '[(let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :some-key :seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\"}]\\\\n                            (m :type))])))\\\\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :some-key]\\\\n           (run-library '[(let [m {:type :cell-ref :id :some-key :seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\"}]\\\\n                            (m :id))]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a runtime-built full-shape map (assoc, not a bound literal) invokes as data\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok :cell-ref]\\\\n           (run-library '[(let [m (assoc (assoc (assoc {} :type :cell-ref)\\\\n                                                :id :some-key)\\\\n                                         :seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\")]\\\\n                            (m :type))]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a full-shape map that is data is not call-eligible\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (is (= [:yin.k/ok false]\\\\n           (run-library '[(yang.call/eligible? {:type :cell-ref :id :some-key\\\\n                                                :seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\"})]))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"genuine references still dereference through admission\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; A cell the engine minted (:cell-0), holding a descriptor with a\\\\n    ;; callable entry: the call reaches the entry.\\\\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\\\\n      (is (= [:yin.k/ok :called]\\\\n             (run-cell-probe (u/app (u/v 'cell/new)\\\\n                                    (u/app (u/v 'assoc) (u/lit {})\\\\n                                           (u/lit :yang.call/entry)\\\\n                                           (u/lam ['invocation] (u/lit :called))))\\\\n                             lane))\\\\n          (str lane \\\\\\\" genuine live\\\\\\\"))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"a genuine-but-dead reference keeps the standing refusal\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; A genuine cell whose contents carry no call entry: admission answers\\\\n    ;; false and the call refuses as not-callable \\u2014 the behavior the D2 bar\\\\n    ;; pins, unchanged by the data fallback.\\\\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\\\\n      (let [[tag payload :as result] (run-cell-probe (u/app (u/v 'cell/new) (u/lit 42))\\\\n                                                     lane)]\\\\n        (is (and (= :yin.k/error tag)\\\\n                 (= :yang.call/not-callable (:yang.call/reason payload)))\\\\n            (str lane \\\\\\\" genuine dead: \\\\\\\" (pr-str result))))))\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"the residual, pinned: a forged id inside the heap language fails closed in the VM\\\\\\\"\\\\n    ;; A map whose :id is a :cell-N keyword and whose seal has the issued\\\\n    ;; format but not the issued content: it is a dereference candidate the\\\\n    ;; VM's heap+seal check rejects \\u2014 a host-level refusal, the same fate\\\\n    ;; any forged reference meets anywhere in the system. No in-language\\\\n    ;; authenticity probe exists (check-ref! throws past every guest catch),\\\\n    ;; so this class stays fail-closed until yin.vm publishes one.\\\\n    (doseq [lane [:walker :semantic]]\\\\n      (is (= [:thrown {:reason :dead-or-forged-reference, :effect :cell/get}]\\\\n             (run-cell-probe (u/lit {:type :cell-ref :id :cell-7\\\\n                                     :seal \\\\\\\"aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\\\\\\\"})\\\\n                             lane))\\\\n          (str lane \\\\\\\" forged in-language id\\\\\\\")))))\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n(deftest test-library-closes-over-its-own-names\\\\n  (testing \\\\\\\"library-for returns the definitions a program mentions, transitively\\\\\\\"\\\\n    (let [names (set (map second (yang/library-for '[(seq? x)])))]\\\\n      (is (every? names '[seq? sequential? vector? map? set? coll?])\\\\n          \\\\\\\"seq? pulls sequential?, vector?, map?, set? and coll?\\\\\\\")\\\\n      (is (not (contains? names 'map))))\\\\ndocs/design/dao.postgraphics.v3.md:23:conformance implies v2 and v1 conformance.\\\\ndocs/design/dao.postgraphics.v3.md:38:consistent with v3's policy for that subset; v3 conformance requires applying\\\\ndocs/design/dao.postgraphics.v3.md:300:V3 fixes the line cap to **butt** for v3 conformance. Butt caps end the stroke\\\\ndocs/design/dao.postgraphics.v3.md:308:V3 fixes the line join to **bevel** for v3 conformance. Bevel joins connect\\\\ndocs/design/dao.postgraphics.v4.md:14:V4 conformance implies v3 conformance, which implies v2 and v1. In particular,\\\\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:74:carries a per-stream conformance policy; each interpreter produces a slice (tuples\\\\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:251:  but downstream interpreters get conformance for free, which is what unlocks\\\\ndocs/design/dao.space.v0.md:270:conformance is an optional realization concern at the member-log boundary, not a\\\\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:427:  by a conformance test, because the rules' `not` clause is quadratic\\\\ndocs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md:7:contracts and conformance oracle stay shared. jolt branches are added only w