holds a sealed `:cursor-ref` naming\\\\n   310\\\\t   it, never the cell itself. Not to be confused with `yin.vm.cell`, the\\\\n   311\\\\t   general heap box. Vocabulary: UCF \\u00a77.5.3, \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Terminology\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".\\\\\\\"\\\\n   312\\\\t  [resource]\\\\n   313\\\\t  (and (map? resource) (contains? resource :stream-id)))\\\\n   314\\\\t\\\\n   315\\\\t\\\\n   316\\\\t(defn issue-ref\\\\n   317\\\\t  \\\\\\\"A reference of `kind` (`:stream-ref`, `:cursor-ref`, or `:cell-ref`) to\\\\n   318\\\\t   resource or heap cell `id`, sealed under the task's capability secret.\\\\n   319\\\\t   A task composed\\\\n   320\\\\t   without a secret cannot issue one: it fails closed rather than issue a\\\\n   321\\\\t   reference anyone could forge.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   322\\\\t  [state kind id]\\\\n   323\\\\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)]\\\\n   324\\\\t    (when (nil? secret)\\\\n   325\\\\t      (fail (str \\\\\\\"This task has no capability secret, so it cannot issue\\\\\\\"\\\\n   326\\\\t                 \\\\\\\" a resource reference\\\\\\\")\\\\n   327\\\\t            {:reason :no-capability-secret, :kind kind, :id id}))\\\\n   328\\\\t    {:type kind, :id id, :seal (seal-of secret kind id)}))\\\\n   329\\\\t\\\\n   330\\\\t\\\\n   331\\\\t(defn authentic-ref?\\\\n   332\\\\t  \\\\\\\"True when `ref` is a `kind` reference this task issued: its seal\\\\n   333\\\\t   verifies under the task's secret, and it names a live resource of that\\\\n   334\\\\t   kind. A `:cell-ref` is checked against `:heap` instead: its id is live\\\\n   335\\\\t   by `contains?` (a cell may hold nil) and its seal equals the one the\\\\n   336\\\\t   heap entry recorded at allocation, so no hash is computed per access.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   337\\\\t  [state kind ref]\\\\n   338\\\\t  (let [secret (:capability-secret state)\\\\n   339\\\\t        id (when (map? ref) (:id ref))]\\\\n   340\\\\t    (if (= :cell-ref kind)\\\\n   341\\\\t      (let [heap (:heap state)]\\\\n   342\\\\t 