ation 1792960000000; refusal fixture `e2e-test` radix-fractional | yang.typescript | the slice completing `%Number.prototype%` (T2 by \\u00a79, or a numbers follow-up) | P3 |\\\\\\\\n| Closed (Stage 0 S3, branch yang-ts-t2b): yang.typescript ordinary functions carried no `prototype` own property; `:normal` function cells now get an eager `prototype` (writable, non-enumerable, non-configurable) with the `constructor` back-link | `object_parity_test/constructors-test` (JVM, four VMs) | yang.typescript | resolved in Stage 0 | P2 |\\\\\\\\n| Closed (Stage 0 S3, branch yang-ts-t2b): yang.typescript every non-arrow callable was constructible; `js/is-constructor?` now reads `:kind` (`:normal`, or `:builtin` flagged `:ctor?`), so `new BigInt(1)`, `new Symbol`, `new String(x)`, arrows, methods and accessors are `TypeError` (wrapper refusal is L-T2-3) | `object_parity_test/constructors-test` | yang.typescript | resolved in Stage 0 | P3 |\\\\\\\\n| yang.typescript: indirect eval (`(0, eval)('1')`, `globalThis.eval`) is not refused at lowering; it reaches the runtime `ReferenceError` from `js/global-get`. Direct `eval` and `new Function` refuse at lowering (T1 R2-fix) | adjudication 1792960000000 \\u00a72 R2-02 | yang.typescript | the slice that gives the global object an `eval` property, if ever; otherwise permanent | P3 |\\\\\\\\n| Closed (Stage 0 S3, branch yang-ts-t2b): yang.typescript `%String.prototype%` had no `toString`/`valueOf`; both now answer the string | `object_parity_test/object-prototype-methods-test` | yang.typescript | resolved in Stage 0 | P3 |\\\\\\\\n| yang.typescript: array index slots are always default data slots; `Object.defineProperty` on an index with a non-default descriptor throws `TypeError` (L-T2-1) | T2 plan R5; prelude make-array comment; `object_parity_test` descriptors | yang.typescript | the slice that gives arrays per-element descriptors, if ever | P3 |\\\\\\\\n| yang.typescript: sparse growth beyond a gap of 2^20 holes throws `RangeError` (